I added the two tests and committed them as b678d42a. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the format check all pass. There's one caveat: the task assumed this risk had only one loud guard, and that turned out to be wrong.

The tests (in src/format/cost/price_audit_tests.rs, which was well under its size limit):
• **every_preset_model_carries_a_price_yoagent_0_25_needs_enable_bundled** checks that every model with a yoagent preset still has a price. There isn't one complete list of those models, so it combines the known-model lists (kept only where they hit a preset) with a named list of 11 ids those lists leave out, including claude-opus-5-5, claude-fable-5-1 and the three GPT-6 models. Each of the 11 must still hit a preset, so a typo there can't quietly drop a model.
• **`the_cost_resolver_returns_the_preset_price_for_opus_5_5** checks that the function /cost uses (model_pricing_with`) returns exactly the preset's price. It checks the preset has a price first, so two missing prices can't pass as equal. It does this for opus-5-5 and then for every model in the set above.
• When either test fails, the message names yoagent::provider::prices::enable_bundled() as the fix.

Deliberate breakages, each changed, run and restored in one command, one at a time, with no leftover changes afterwards:
• **A — /cost skips the preset price: the second test failed by name. 10 existing tests** failed too.
• **B — every preset loses its price (what 0.25 does if `enable_bundled()` is forgotten): both new tests failed by name. 22 existing tests** failed too, including every_preset_id_is_priced_by_its_own_constructor, which already checks that each preset has a price.

So the upgrade could not have landed this regression with everything green; 22 tests already guard it. What the new tests add is the diagnosis: none of those 22 failure messages says what the fix is, and a wall of unexplained price mismatches makes it tempting to weaken the tests instead. I rewrote the test file's header comment so it says this, and the commit message records the 10 and 22.

I didn't change any docs because no behaviour changed. The upgrade itself, #997, #1003 and #1004 are untouched.
